  "reading": "The per-verify cost ratio does not grow with height. ECDSA moves from 2.087\u00d7 through height 49999 to 2.054\u00d7 from 50000 through 99999, and Schnorr from 2.099\u00d7 to 2.012\u00d7. The Taproot tweak moves from 1.745\u00d7 to 1.600\u00d7. The mix does shift: through height 49999 the verifications are 92% ECDSA, and from 50000 through 99999 they are 52% Schnorr, 27% ECDSA, and 22% tweaks. Schnorr costs about the same ratio as ECDSA, so that shift does not raise the penalty. The script_verify wall ratio still rises from 1.532\u00d7 to 1.868\u00d7 because the later windows fill the worker threads: own_curve verify time is 7.53\u00d7 the wall-clock script bucket after height 50000, against 5.30\u00d7 before, with 8 script threads. Counts match on both backends. There is one script job per input overall (27818301). The split does not record inputs per window, so it cannot say whether the jump in verifications per block after height 50000 is more inputs or more signatures per input. Pubkey parsing sits inside the ECDSA and Schnorr calls.",
